### Fixed

- Fixed `seqfu cat --basename --part` so invalid part indexes now fail cleanly instead of reading invalid memory.
- Fixed `seqfu cat --max-ns` to match its help text: records are discarded only when they contain more than the requested number of Ns.
- Improved `seqfu cat` trimming so the default path no longer copies sequence and quality strings unnecessarily.

### Documentation

- Clarified that `seqfu cat --max-bp` is applied separately to each input file.
- Clarified how `seqfu cat` handles mixed FASTA/FASTQ input and when to use `--fasta` or `--fastq`.

--

### Fixed

- Fixed `fu-index` CASAVA comment parsing for read, filter, control, and index fields.
- Made `--min-ratio` inclusive, so values exactly at the threshold now pass.
- Made missing input files and invalid `--max-reads` / `--min-ratio` values return non-zero.
- Updated `fu-index` to count reads in streaming mode instead of buffering sampled records.
